3.equals() : It is an instance method and comparre 2 Strings(calling and arguement)
In case sensitive way. It then returns true if the strings are same otherwise it returns false.

Ex
String s1=new String("Hello");
String s2=new String("Hello");
String s3=new String("hello");

System.out.println(s1.equals(s2));//true
System.out.println(s1.equals(s3));//false


==================================================================================================


